course: dictionary
lesson: 2467
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «She sat by the fire, darning a hole in her sock.» Sewing is the clue here, so darn means to mend a hole by stitching threads across it.
explain: Darn can also be a mild word people say when they are cross. «He dropped his toast and cried, "Darn it!"» Nobody is sewing. The word shows he is annoyed, and it is a polite stand-in for a ruder word.
explain: Darn can also mean very or annoying, and it comes before another word. «That darn cat keeps climbing the curtains.» Try the swap: "that annoying cat" still makes sense, so darn means annoying here.
fact: Context helps you choose the right meaning of a word with more than one meaning.
fact: «Darn» means to mend a hole by sewing threads across it.
fact: «Darn!» or «Darn it!» is a mild word said when you are annoyed, instead of a stronger word.
fact: «Darn» or «darned» can mean very or annoying, as in «a darn good idea».
fact: Darn is informal, so it is most often heard in everyday talk and children's stories.
exercise: «She sat by the fire, darning a hole in her sock.» What does darning mean here? | Buying a new pair | *Mending a hole by sewing | Washing the sock in hot water | Painting a pattern on it
exercise: «Darn!» cried Tom when he dropped his toast. What is Tom feeling? | Sleepy | Very hungry | *Annoyed | Delighted
exercise: «That darn cat keeps climbing the curtains.» What does darn mean in this sentence? | Hidden under the bed | Kind and gentle | Made of wool | *Very annoying
test: Which word is the odd one out, not a mild stand-in for a swear word? | Drat | *Thread | Fudge | Blast
test: «He darned his socks every Sunday night.» What did he do with his socks? | Threw them away | *Mended the holes | Bought new ones | Dyed them red
exam: Grandma dropped her cup and cried, «Gosh darn it!» What does this show? | She is pleased with the cup | *She is cross, but in a polite way | She is very tired | She is learning to sew
